# BEAT 30 — a bang that reaches its agent. `@omar !cmd` in the room runs in
# omar's directory, is drawn in omar's thread, and goes to omar as Claude Code's
# own bash-mode record - a turn omar answers. harbor/web/statuses.sh is a real
# check, so the output on camera is what it printed.
Output .work/out/30-bang.mp4
Source .work/head.tape
Hide
Source .work/stage.tape
Show
Sleep 1500ms
Type "@omar !sh statuses.sh"
Sleep 800ms
Enter
Sleep 10s

# omar's thread: the command, its output and the answer, together.
Type "@omar"
Sleep 4s
Backspace 5
Sleep 1500ms
